WEBVTT

01:02.119 --> 01:04.297
[A tip about Head of Audit Joo In Ah]
Joo In Ah...

01:04.297 --> 01:05.296
[Joo In Ah is in an inappropriate relationship
with a coworker]

01:05.296 --> 01:07.110
Is she having an affair?

01:09.539 --> 01:11.829
[Joo In Ah]

01:12.625 --> 01:14.294
Just hear me out.

01:14.294 --> 01:16.789
This is really unfair.

01:16.789 --> 01:17.939
I said no at first.

01:17.939 --> 01:21.217
But the vendor said
it's basically industry standard.

01:21.217 --> 01:22.260
Head Joo,

01:22.260 --> 01:24.561
Head Joo, with all due respect.

01:24.561 --> 01:27.603
Please.

01:27.603 --> 01:29.820
I'm begging you. Just this once.

01:29.820 --> 01:34.950
My kids are still young,
and my wife quit her job to raise them.

01:34.950 --> 01:37.054
Please.

01:37.890 --> 01:41.114
You should've thought about your family
before taking the kickback.

01:41.114 --> 01:43.149
Don't use them as a sob story now.

01:43.149 --> 01:44.559
What?

02:02.916 --> 02:04.564
Don't push it.

02:04.564 --> 02:08.297
Even a rat bites when it's cornered.

02:17.350 --> 02:19.293
Damn it!

02:25.572 --> 02:27.879
What, you here for the show?

02:29.245 --> 02:32.911
You weren't actually hoping he'd hit me,
were you?

02:43.042 --> 02:45.567
She's ruthless.

02:48.974 --> 02:51.099
That ruthless woman had an affair?

02:51.099 --> 02:52.138
No way.

02:52.138 --> 02:54.325
Assistant Manager Noh.

02:57.672 --> 02:59.272
Yes?

03:02.404 --> 03:04.780
You said you had something to tell me.

03:05.405 --> 03:06.445
Oh, well...

03:06.445 --> 03:10.135
Alright, until I figure out what's going on,

03:10.135 --> 03:12.561
strategic retreat.

03:13.541 --> 03:16.125
I wanted to apologize.

03:16.125 --> 03:19.160
I was out of line at karaoke yesterday.

03:19.814 --> 03:22.734
I'm really sorry, ma'am.

03:27.981 --> 03:29.868
Well...

03:29.868 --> 03:32.478
I guess I wasn't very considerate either.

03:32.478 --> 03:35.983
I kept an ace like you
stuck doing limited work.

03:35.983 --> 03:38.366
Must've been frustrating.

03:40.403 --> 03:41.568
Okay.

03:41.568 --> 03:44.830
I'll give you more responsibility.

04:00.843 --> 04:03.001
Oh, wait.

04:03.001 --> 04:05.954
Why are you doing this?

04:06.954 --> 04:08.633
Gosh.

04:08.633 --> 04:11.554
Oh, I mean...

04:11.554 --> 04:14.841
why'd you go off on her yesterday?

04:15.854 --> 04:18.138
Seriously, be careful.

04:18.138 --> 04:19.656
After seeing what happened to
General Manager Seo,

04:19.656 --> 04:22.024
Now I get why people call her "MJYS."

04:22.024 --> 04:24.974
"Mess with Joo In Ah
and you're completely screwed."

04:24.974 --> 04:27.684
"M-J-Y-S!"

04:27.684 --> 04:29.481
[MJYS]

04:29.481 --> 04:31.854
Man, just thinking about it...

04:31.854 --> 04:33.867
Anyway,

04:34.679 --> 04:35.976
Could you take this too?

04:35.976 --> 04:37.329
While you're at it.

04:37.329 --> 04:39.688
You know I'm rooting for you, right?

04:39.688 --> 04:41.327
You got this!

05:09.484 --> 05:11.241
Darn it.

05:47.459 --> 05:50.445
MJYS, my ass.

05:50.445 --> 05:53.792
We're all just salaried workers anyway.

05:54.532 --> 05:56.076
[A tip about Head of Audit Joo In Ah]

05:56.076 --> 05:59.005
[Joo In Ah is in an inappropriate relationship
with a coworker]

06:00.907 --> 06:02.191
Alright.

06:02.191 --> 06:06.111
If that tip turns out to be true,

06:06.111 --> 06:09.949
I'll be holding the card
that can take her down.

06:09.949 --> 06:16.051
This might be the chance I've been waiting for.

06:16.051 --> 06:18.441
Fine, Joo In Ah.

06:18.441 --> 06:20.897
Let's see how this plays out.

06:20.897 --> 06:24.475
We'll find out who ends up ruined.

06:36.746 --> 06:40.006
[Episode 3: A Woman Full of Surprises]

06:45.079 --> 06:47.669
The office is a battlefield.

06:47.669 --> 06:51.764
Every day, we fight to survive and win.

06:53.024 --> 06:56.027
The first rule of any fight
is knowing who's on your side.

06:56.027 --> 06:58.947
Telling friend from foe.

07:00.213 --> 07:02.077
But...

07:02.077 --> 07:03.635
Good morning, ma'am.

07:03.635 --> 07:06.060
Oh, you dyed your hair.

07:06.060 --> 07:07.979
You look 20 years younger.

07:07.979 --> 07:09.718
Oh, hi there.

07:09.718 --> 07:11.901
Mr. Sang Hyun, did you drink a lot yesterday?

07:11.901 --> 07:12.961
Go get some hangover soup.

07:12.961 --> 07:15.032
At work, telling friend from foe...

07:15.032 --> 07:17.969
- Keep up the good work.
- isn't so easy.

07:17.969 --> 07:20.328
Sometimes your enemy shows up
wearing a friendly face.

07:20.328 --> 07:23.472
Been busy lately? We should catch up soon.

07:23.472 --> 07:26.329
HR and Audit should be sharing info, you know?

07:26.329 --> 07:28.206
Sounds good.

07:28.206 --> 07:31.045
Let's grab a drink sometime.

07:31.045 --> 07:32.997
I love it.

07:32.997 --> 07:35.160
Alright, take care.

07:36.089 --> 07:37.487
Oh, ma'am...

07:37.487 --> 07:40.480
Today's ally can be tomorrow's enemy.

07:40.480 --> 07:42.358
You're hauling all that by yourself?

07:42.358 --> 07:45.779
Just getting in? I do this every day. I'm fine.

07:45.779 --> 07:47.056
But...

07:47.056 --> 07:49.159
Careful. You'll throw your back out.

07:49.159 --> 07:51.336
Don't worry about my back.

07:51.336 --> 07:53.869
You know, this isn't about strength.
It's technique.

07:53.869 --> 07:56.869
Like this. Like this.

07:57.506 --> 08:00.066
That's scientific.

08:00.066 --> 08:03.019
Still, it feels good having you around.

08:12.068 --> 08:14.531
But one thing's for sure.

08:14.531 --> 08:16.931
The moment I decide someone's the enemy,

08:16.931 --> 08:19.697
they become one.

08:29.819 --> 08:31.470
Now

08:31.470 --> 08:34.150
I'll keep my blade hidden

08:34.150 --> 08:36.467
and wait for the perfect strike

08:36.467 --> 08:40.445
[A tip about Head of Audit Joo In Ah]
against my number one target, Joo In Ah.

08:42.249 --> 08:44.577
Head Joo requested

08:44.577 --> 08:48.135
to be excluded from executive meetings
going forward?

08:48.135 --> 08:49.177
Yes.

08:49.177 --> 08:53.330
The Haemu Audit is audit in name only.
There's no real independence.

08:53.330 --> 08:55.480
We need to fix the reporting structure first.

08:55.480 --> 08:59.454
Right now,
we're completely subordinate to management.

08:59.454 --> 09:02.504
That's not easy for me to hear.

09:02.504 --> 09:04.992
I don't think I can approve that.

09:04.992 --> 09:07.034
I'd actually prefer

09:07.635 --> 09:10.182
you stay under us.

09:13.252 --> 09:16.359
I'd appreciate your consideration.

09:16.359 --> 09:20.700
I have a backlog to get through,
so I'll excuse myself.

09:28.772 --> 09:30.577
Looks pretty independent.

09:30.577 --> 09:32.567
Next, HR.

09:36.662 --> 09:38.079
Well...

09:38.079 --> 09:40.516
The Chairman requested

09:40.516 --> 09:43.347
that Executive Jeon Seong Yeol
be brought back to HQ.

09:43.347 --> 09:46.534
[Special Executive Personnel Report]
He called me personally this morning.

09:46.534 --> 09:47.621
Yes.

09:47.621 --> 09:49.239
I'm aware.

09:50.086 --> 09:51.670
Yeah, of course.

09:51.670 --> 09:54.263
I figured you would be,

09:54.263 --> 09:56.273
Vice Chairman.

09:56.273 --> 10:00.520
Still, you should've run it by me
before submitting for approval.

10:00.520 --> 10:03.047
For something like this.

10:03.047 --> 10:06.453
My apologies. That was my oversight.

10:06.453 --> 10:08.797
Personally,

10:08.797 --> 10:11.444
I'm concerned about

10:11.444 --> 10:17.370
the risk of bringing him back right after
his suspended sentence ended.

10:22.531 --> 10:24.670
Is that the Chairman?

10:29.599 --> 10:31.279
[Chairman]

10:37.679 --> 10:40.403
Yeah, Father. It's Jae Yeol.

10:40.403 --> 10:41.600
Did I dial the wrong number?

10:41.600 --> 10:44.773
My apologies.
We're in a meeting, so I picked up.

10:44.773 --> 10:47.217
If you've seen it, sign it and send it up.

10:47.217 --> 10:48.913
About that...

10:51.030 --> 10:53.563
HR has raised some concerns.

10:53.563 --> 10:55.374
It may be a bit too soon.

10:55.374 --> 10:57.316
There could be backlash,
saying it's just for show.

10:57.316 --> 10:58.920
You seen construction stocks lately?

10:58.920 --> 11:00.743
Give credit where it's due.

11:00.743 --> 11:03.070
Don't make me repeat myself.

11:18.361 --> 11:20.258
Good work, everyone.

11:20.258 --> 11:23.656
- See you tomorrow.
- Good work.

11:25.249 --> 11:27.060
Anyone up for dinner?

11:27.060 --> 11:29.886
My wife said I can eat out.

11:30.780 --> 11:32.470
No one?

11:32.470 --> 11:34.804
- See you tomorrow.
- Have a good night, sir.

11:34.804 --> 11:35.838
Guess not.

11:35.838 --> 11:38.164
Everyone's dieting or what?

11:38.164 --> 11:39.480
Alright.

11:39.480 --> 11:41.548
Okay, got it.

11:57.896 --> 11:58.940
[Recording begins]

11:59.593 --> 12:02.960
Project "No Name." Target follow, initiated.

12:35.076 --> 12:37.671
Heading straight home?

13:27.804 --> 13:29.566
[Items Purchased]
Triangle kimbap,

13:29.566 --> 13:31.343
a can of beer,

13:32.174 --> 13:34.327
and antacids?

13:39.345 --> 13:41.372
Beats me.

13:43.384 --> 13:44.772
Hey, Mister.

13:44.772 --> 13:47.499
Are you a stalker? You broke or something?

13:50.882 --> 13:52.092
Did you hear?

13:52.092 --> 13:54.302
Executive Jeon Seong Yeol,
the Vice Chairman's brother,

13:54.302 --> 13:56.198
is coming back to HQ.

13:56.198 --> 14:00.268
I heard the Chairman favors him
over the Vice Chairman.

14:00.268 --> 14:02.845
Probably because he's the son he had
with his current wife.

14:02.845 --> 14:04.271
This is top secret, but...

14:04.271 --> 14:06.476
Vice Chairman Jeon Jae Yeol's mother.

14:06.476 --> 14:09.482
I heard she was basically forced out
because of mental illness.

14:09.482 --> 14:12.066
They say she was a disgrace to the family.

14:12.856 --> 14:15.679
There's even talk about it being hereditary.

14:15.679 --> 14:17.704
- Then the Vice...
- Come on.

14:17.704 --> 14:21.642
Why are you young guys so quick to judge?

14:21.642 --> 14:24.479
All we need to think about is this.

14:24.479 --> 14:28.145
When Executive Jeon comes back,
which side are we going to be on?

14:28.145 --> 14:30.029
Honestly,

14:30.029 --> 14:33.022
it's probably better to side with
Executive Jeon, right?

14:33.022 --> 14:38.160
The Vice Chairman's just a title anyway.
He doesn't even have any shares.

14:41.615 --> 14:43.677
Hold on.

14:43.677 --> 14:45.274
Not so fast.

14:45.274 --> 14:48.714
The Vice Chairman's got backing from his wife.

14:48.714 --> 14:50.838
Her family is Sejang Group.

14:50.838 --> 14:53.520
The Chairman arranged
that marriage for a reason.

14:53.520 --> 14:55.378
You can't ignore that kind of power.

14:55.378 --> 14:56.642
That's true.

14:56.642 --> 14:58.421
Then it's really hard to tell.

14:58.421 --> 14:59.798
One thing's for sure.

14:59.798 --> 15:04.015
A massive storm is coming to this company soon.

15:04.015 --> 15:06.555
Watch your backs.

15:11.517 --> 15:13.048
Sir?

15:13.048 --> 15:14.755
- Come here a second.
- What is it?

15:14.755 --> 15:15.880
Come here.

15:15.880 --> 15:17.131
What?

15:18.328 --> 15:20.119
Take this with you.

15:20.119 --> 15:21.304
What is it?

15:21.304 --> 15:25.675
It's from the executive meal.
We had a lot left over.

15:25.675 --> 15:28.045
Your wife's raising twins.

15:28.045 --> 15:30.316
That's a lot on her plate.

15:30.316 --> 15:32.344
Just take it home.

15:32.344 --> 15:36.399
Thanks to you,
I get to try executive food for once.

15:38.043 --> 15:39.647
And this too.

15:39.647 --> 15:41.740
It's not much. Get the kids some clothes.

15:41.740 --> 15:43.444
No, no. They've got plenty of clothes.

15:43.444 --> 15:48.208
You gave way too much when my father passed.

15:48.208 --> 15:50.181
I didn't even get to thank you properly.
Just take it.

15:50.181 --> 15:51.719
It really wasn't much. It's fine.

15:51.719 --> 15:54.239
- Come on.
- No, I can't take this.

15:54.239 --> 15:56.714
- No, you have to.
- Ma'am, stop.

15:56.714 --> 15:58.554
I said don't.

15:58.554 --> 16:00.412
What is that?

16:03.209 --> 16:05.435
What am I looking at?

16:08.295 --> 16:10.139
No way.

16:10.139 --> 16:12.225
This is insane.

16:36.024 --> 16:38.774
One triangle kimbap, one can of beer.

16:38.774 --> 16:40.820
That's all she ever gets, right?

16:41.637 --> 16:45.471
I thought she just didn't eat much.

16:45.471 --> 16:47.390
I see.

16:50.087 --> 16:53.062
Not really into food, I guess.

16:55.435 --> 16:57.839
Hey, by the way...

16:57.839 --> 17:00.329
Does she ever come with a guy?

17:00.329 --> 17:02.966
No, never seen that. Or with a girl either.

17:02.966 --> 17:04.346
She's always alone.

17:04.346 --> 17:05.770
Really?

17:08.172 --> 17:09.206
By the way,

17:09.206 --> 17:11.163
you've got a good memory.

17:11.163 --> 17:12.687
You remember your customers well.

17:12.687 --> 17:14.900
No, it's just her I remember.

17:14.900 --> 17:17.077
Just her? Why?

17:17.077 --> 17:18.340
Because she's pretty.

17:18.340 --> 17:19.405
What? "Pretty?"

17:19.405 --> 17:22.056
You mean... her?

17:32.345 --> 17:36.115
Yeah, I guess beauty's subjective.

17:36.115 --> 17:39.407
She must be your type.

17:45.852 --> 17:47.735
Want another ice cream?

17:47.735 --> 17:49.704
No. Buy me wine.

17:52.762 --> 17:56.768
- Rina, I've got my car...
- I'm drinking it with my boyfriend.

17:59.426 --> 18:02.386
Where to, my princesses?

18:03.133 --> 18:04.723
Where should we go?

18:04.723 --> 18:08.443
- This way.
- This way? Here we go.

18:10.017 --> 18:11.433
This is the ocean.

18:11.433 --> 18:13.261
Where to now?

18:13.261 --> 18:14.916
Backwards?

18:18.955 --> 18:20.058
Where are we going?

18:20.058 --> 18:21.394
Which way?

18:21.394 --> 18:23.804
- This way?
- Girls.

18:23.804 --> 18:27.161
It's past your bedtime.
Go inside and brush your teeth.

18:27.161 --> 18:29.367
The mommy monster's mad. Run!

18:29.367 --> 18:31.977
Run for your lives!

18:31.977 --> 18:33.673
Run...

18:35.004 --> 18:37.414
Man. Raising kids at my age is no joke.

18:37.414 --> 18:39.118
Take it easy.

18:39.118 --> 18:41.488
You still have to make money
until they're through college.

18:41.488 --> 18:43.586
Yeah.

18:46.776 --> 18:48.879
Honey.

18:48.879 --> 18:52.434
This food's so good. Big company perks, huh?

18:52.434 --> 18:54.102
You like it?

18:54.102 --> 18:57.315
Maybe it's better because I didn't cook.

18:57.315 --> 18:58.512
Enjoy.

18:58.512 --> 19:00.900
Bring some home more often, honey.

19:00.900 --> 19:02.731
Alright.

19:03.947 --> 19:06.157
Seeing you enjoy it makes me happy.

19:06.157 --> 19:07.666
Here.

19:14.363 --> 19:16.195
You're back?

19:16.195 --> 19:17.663
You're late.

19:17.663 --> 19:19.983
Had plans?

19:19.983 --> 19:21.976
No, just overtime.

19:26.180 --> 19:28.256
Why'd you buy so much from a convenience store?

19:28.256 --> 19:30.173
Oh, that?

19:30.173 --> 19:32.822
The clerk shook me down.

19:34.676 --> 19:37.127
Ten condoms?

19:37.127 --> 19:38.666
What?

19:42.025 --> 19:44.162
Seriously? She's just a kid.

19:44.162 --> 19:45.739
Do her parents even know?

19:45.739 --> 19:48.235
They sent her abroad for school
and she's doing this?

19:48.235 --> 19:53.180
Relax. Sounds like she got good sex education.

19:53.815 --> 19:57.354
Ten of them? Someone's love life is on fire.

19:59.500 --> 20:01.608
That's nothing, come on.

20:01.608 --> 20:03.259
I just...

20:03.259 --> 20:05.076
I mean...

20:15.387 --> 20:17.890
Anyway, you need to eat better than that.

20:17.890 --> 20:19.234
Just order something.

20:19.234 --> 20:22.282
I already had dinner.
This is a late-night snack.

20:23.556 --> 20:24.778
Want one?

20:24.778 --> 20:26.619
It was buy one, get one.

20:39.655 --> 20:41.285
What kind of person eats

20:41.285 --> 20:44.477
just one triangle kimbap
for dinner every night?

20:46.018 --> 20:47.632
What does that say about them?

20:47.632 --> 20:49.244
Probably someone broke.

20:49.244 --> 20:50.880
No, not really.

20:51.584 --> 20:53.469
They actually make good money.

20:55.404 --> 20:57.063
Then...

20:58.057 --> 21:00.013
someone who just eats to survive?

21:00.013 --> 21:03.928
Like, they eat because they have to,
not because they want to.

21:03.928 --> 21:06.706
Even if they seem to have it all,

21:06.706 --> 21:09.589
they're empty inside.

21:09.589 --> 21:11.093
So

21:11.093 --> 21:13.726
even when they eat,
it doesn't feel like eating,

21:13.726 --> 21:16.701
and even when they sleep,
it doesn't feel like resting.

21:22.238 --> 21:24.209
Who are you talking about?

21:24.209 --> 21:27.436
Better not be you,
living off midnight snacks like that.

21:32.010 --> 21:33.154
Hello, Seung Hee.

21:33.154 --> 21:34.180
Hey.

21:34.180 --> 21:36.201
Sorry to call so late,

21:36.201 --> 21:38.071
but have you seen the company anonymous board?

21:38.071 --> 21:41.584
Posts about the Vice Chairman
and Executive Jeon keep coming up.

21:42.522 --> 21:46.756
[Haemu War: legendary situation unfolding]
[J and S have different moms?]

21:49.570 --> 21:51.286
Information Office!

21:51.286 --> 21:53.736
Do something about this!

21:53.736 --> 21:56.436
Take the posts down immediately.

21:56.436 --> 21:58.109
Block keywords if you have to.

21:58.109 --> 22:00.247
Make it so people can't even type
things like "biological mother!"

22:00.247 --> 22:03.299
They'll just get around it with abbreviations.

22:03.299 --> 22:05.276
And if we block too much,

22:05.276 --> 22:08.652
HR will get backlash
for controlling public opinion.

22:08.652 --> 22:12.794
And "CompanyLife.com..."
That's out of our control to begin with.

22:13.675 --> 22:15.758
Come on.

22:15.758 --> 22:17.880
I'm not telling you to control it.

22:18.525 --> 22:21.137
Is that really the only way?

22:21.958 --> 22:25.355
You know, people only have one mouth.

22:25.355 --> 22:29.626
Think of something. Think!

22:34.240 --> 22:37.081
This is driving me crazy.

22:37.081 --> 22:38.368
Sir.

22:38.368 --> 22:39.398
Yeah?

22:39.398 --> 22:40.935
Could you take a look at this?

22:40.935 --> 22:42.368
What?

22:42.975 --> 22:45.244
This was posted yesterday.

22:46.312 --> 22:48.696
What if we play it up a bit?

22:48.696 --> 22:50.755
Might draw some attention.

22:50.755 --> 22:52.726
"A middle-aged romance?"

22:52.726 --> 22:54.342
Hold on.

22:54.342 --> 22:58.184
That jawline looks familiar.

22:59.307 --> 23:01.427
Team Leader Moo?

23:03.370 --> 23:04.462
Nice one.

23:04.462 --> 23:06.274
Just a moment.

23:06.274 --> 23:09.104
Let's go with this.

23:09.104 --> 23:10.568
So...

23:10.568 --> 23:14.587
"Guy Who's Into Older Women."

23:16.043 --> 23:17.774
Or...

23:17.774 --> 23:21.653
"Team Leader of Audit's Affair..."
That hit harder?

23:21.653 --> 23:24.122
But exposing personal info might be a bit...

23:24.122 --> 23:27.469
That's what gives it impact.

23:27.469 --> 23:29.813
And don't worry too much.

23:29.813 --> 23:32.286
He's a PNU anyway.

23:32.942 --> 23:34.458
"PNU?"

23:35.226 --> 23:37.403
Yeah, it's an HR term.

23:37.403 --> 23:40.503
"Person of no use."

23:40.503 --> 23:42.573
Means exactly what it sounds like.

23:42.573 --> 23:44.971
That's harsh.

23:44.971 --> 23:48.760
When a report has this many pages,
you fold the corner like this.

23:48.760 --> 23:52.539
Makes it easier for the higher-ups.

23:57.932 --> 23:59.801
- What?
- Nothing.

23:59.801 --> 24:01.719
That's how I made it to team leader.

24:01.719 --> 24:04.003
Guess that's why I'm still just a manager.

24:14.382 --> 24:17.787
[Joo In Ah]

24:17.787 --> 24:19.698
[Haemu Group HR Profile: Joo In Ah]

24:23.557 --> 24:25.970
[No Cultural / Leisure Expense Records]

24:27.477 --> 24:28.897
[No Paid Leave Taken]

24:28.897 --> 24:30.086
[No Corporate Card Usage]

24:43.758 --> 24:45.524
She never takes time off...

24:45.524 --> 24:47.064
doesn't use any benefits...

24:47.064 --> 24:49.064
barely eats...

24:49.916 --> 24:52.712
What does she even live for?

24:56.769 --> 24:58.213
Startled you, didn't I?

24:58.213 --> 25:00.397
You almost jumped out of your skin.

25:00.397 --> 25:02.324
Is this what you do for fun?

25:02.324 --> 25:04.063
That worked.

25:05.205 --> 25:09.088
Wow, you're the one taking care of it?

25:09.088 --> 25:10.458
Yes.

25:10.458 --> 25:12.925
I just keep it around sometimes.

25:12.925 --> 25:16.602
You're surprisingly thoughtful.

25:16.602 --> 25:18.384
It's pretty.

25:20.255 --> 25:22.275
It even smells nice.

25:33.457 --> 25:35.481
Because she's pretty.

25:35.481 --> 25:36.798
Well...

25:36.798 --> 25:38.900
it's not like she's not pretty.

25:39.565 --> 25:41.732
Wait.

25:41.732 --> 25:44.582
Did you just smile looking at me?

25:44.582 --> 25:46.339
Oh, I just...

25:46.339 --> 25:49.019
Do I look funny to you, Assistant Manager Noh?

25:49.019 --> 25:52.354
No, it's just...
what you did earlier was funny.

25:52.354 --> 25:54.453
The way you startled me.

25:54.453 --> 25:57.806
The more I think about it, the funnier it gets.

25:57.806 --> 26:01.366
The more I look at you,
the more I see how witty you are.

26:03.074 --> 26:06.126
Oh, you noticed?

26:06.126 --> 26:08.467
You've got good instincts.

26:08.467 --> 26:12.144
I don't get why everyone says I'm scary.
I'm actually a lot of fun.

26:12.144 --> 26:13.644
Right?

26:13.644 --> 26:14.888
Yes.

26:14.888 --> 26:17.085
You've got good sense.

26:22.248 --> 26:25.774
Man, I need a sugar fix.

26:26.868 --> 26:32.369
Where's Ms. Yoon's snack stash?

26:32.369 --> 26:34.119
What?

26:34.119 --> 26:36.710
It's still here, right?

26:36.710 --> 26:38.414
You know, the candy box.

26:38.414 --> 26:40.350
Chocolate and stuff.

26:40.350 --> 26:42.222
Why won't this open?

26:43.154 --> 26:44.709
Wait...

26:44.709 --> 26:47.730
Have you been hiding it from me on purpose?

26:47.730 --> 26:50.327
If you didn't want me taking from it,
you should've just said so.

26:50.327 --> 26:54.093
Locking it up like this? Now I feel awkward.

26:54.093 --> 26:56.643
I've been making it pretty obvious.

26:56.643 --> 26:59.230
You just didn't pick up on it.

26:59.998 --> 27:02.170
Oh, I'm sorry.

27:02.170 --> 27:03.815
What?

27:05.096 --> 27:08.869
Sir, you might want to see this.

27:10.223 --> 27:13.377
[Doing this out in the company cafeteria?]
[So scandalous]

27:15.889 --> 27:18.830
Team Leader Moo, you're trending.

27:23.653 --> 27:25.190
[Guy Who's Into Older Women, this is crazy]
"Guy Who's Into Older Women?"

27:25.190 --> 27:27.670
Looks like you've got a nickname now.

27:27.670 --> 27:29.960
I've got a fun one like that too.

27:29.960 --> 27:31.694
No, no.

27:31.694 --> 27:34.364
Why would I be into older women?

27:34.364 --> 27:38.865
That photo... it's just the angle.
It looks misleading.

27:38.865 --> 27:44.410
There's really nothing going on
between me and her.

27:44.410 --> 27:46.554
No way...

27:46.554 --> 27:49.320
Hell just froze over.

27:49.320 --> 27:53.636
This isn't something you can just laugh off.

27:55.307 --> 27:56.937
Assistant Manager Ahn.

27:56.937 --> 27:58.613
Yes?

28:03.304 --> 28:05.934
You'll handle this.

28:05.934 --> 28:08.218
Assistant Manager Noh was the PM,

28:08.218 --> 28:10.551
but since he's on the same team,
it's not appropriate.

28:10.551 --> 28:12.655
Wait, I'm investigating... what exactly?

28:12.655 --> 28:15.035
Team Leader Moo Gwang Il's case.

28:16.836 --> 28:18.480
You're opening an investigation?

28:18.480 --> 28:22.107
Of course.
It's big enough to blow up the company board.

28:22.107 --> 28:24.717
But this is just a misunderstanding.

28:24.717 --> 28:26.251
It's not even a case.

28:26.251 --> 28:28.708
I'm completely innocent. You know me.

28:28.708 --> 28:32.834
Yes, you can explain that
during the investigation.

28:32.834 --> 28:35.804
Until then, you'll be stepping down
from your duties.

28:35.804 --> 28:40.238
Manager Cha Seong Tae
will take over approvals for Team 3.

28:41.851 --> 28:43.254
That's all.

28:53.701 --> 28:55.219
What are you all standing around for?

28:55.219 --> 28:56.226
Dismissed.

28:57.914 --> 29:00.114
This isn't right.

29:00.114 --> 29:02.210
This really isn't right.

29:51.473 --> 29:53.694
I'm home.

29:57.286 --> 29:59.155
Everyone asleep?

30:00.226 --> 30:01.913
Are the kids asleep?

30:11.637 --> 30:13.991
This is you, right?

30:17.604 --> 30:19.728
Don't tell me...

30:19.728 --> 30:24.687
the food I ate yesterday was from her.

30:27.121 --> 30:29.718
- Yeah?
- Well, that was...

30:31.181 --> 30:34.334
Gosh, how do I even explain this?

30:44.379 --> 30:46.496
The way she handles things,

30:46.496 --> 30:49.280
she doesn't seem like someone who'd slip up.

30:52.141 --> 30:54.491
Am I just wasting my time?

31:00.426 --> 31:01.477
What?

31:01.477 --> 31:03.317
She's not going home?

31:03.317 --> 31:04.687
Gosh.

32:18.992 --> 32:20.157
Okay,

32:20.157 --> 32:21.694
there she is.

32:39.892 --> 32:42.163
[Today's Art Class, 9:00 p.m.]
Art class?

32:45.342 --> 32:47.239
Excuse me.

32:47.239 --> 32:49.359
Are you going in?

32:49.359 --> 32:51.780
Oh, no. Sorry.

32:59.037 --> 33:01.624
She's into painting?

33:11.355 --> 33:13.773
- Hello.
- Good morning.

33:17.379 --> 33:19.136
Gosh, you scared me.

33:19.136 --> 33:21.054
Sir?

33:21.054 --> 33:23.409
Oh, sorry.

33:33.185 --> 33:35.339
Surprise.

33:37.545 --> 33:40.463
Wait... did you sleep here?

33:40.463 --> 33:42.263
Did you fight with your wife or something?

33:42.263 --> 33:44.571
You could've used the overnight room.

33:44.571 --> 33:46.655
Why are you here, Team Leader Moo?

33:46.655 --> 33:48.224
Oh, hello.

33:48.224 --> 33:51.768
I had some things come up last night
and couldn't go home.

33:51.768 --> 33:54.172
Couldn't think of anywhere else to go.

33:54.172 --> 33:56.468
So you chose the office?

33:58.899 --> 34:02.242
You really don't draw boundaries, do you?

34:02.242 --> 34:06.132
You eat company food outside
and sleep inside the office.

34:09.150 --> 34:10.893
Please leave.

34:10.893 --> 34:12.390
Right now.

34:12.390 --> 34:13.418
Sorry?

34:13.418 --> 34:17.064
A subject under investigation is not allowed
unrestricted access to the office.

34:17.064 --> 34:20.374
For the Team Leader of Audit,
that's pretty careless, don't you think?

34:20.374 --> 34:21.842
Ms. Pyeon,

34:21.842 --> 34:25.478
submit a request to restrict
Team Leader Moo's access to the Audit.

34:25.478 --> 34:29.064
- Isn't that a bit...
- That is company policy.

34:30.112 --> 34:32.498
And Audit exists to enforce it.

34:32.498 --> 34:34.293
Yes.

34:34.293 --> 34:37.906
That was my mistake. I'll leave right away.

34:37.906 --> 34:39.834
I'm sorry.

34:39.834 --> 34:42.394
Just my shoes. One second.

34:42.394 --> 34:43.538
Sorry.

34:43.538 --> 34:46.855
Ms. Pyeon, please hold onto my ID.

34:46.855 --> 34:49.186
Hyun Gyu, can you move this box for me?

34:49.186 --> 34:50.531
I'm sorry.

34:50.531 --> 34:52.159
I'm really sorry.

34:52.159 --> 34:53.382
My apologies.

34:53.382 --> 34:54.826
Sorry.

35:12.610 --> 35:14.478
You're Moo Gwang Il, right?

35:14.478 --> 35:15.934
Yes, who are you?

35:15.934 --> 35:17.257
Don't recognize me?

35:17.257 --> 35:20.014
We met at my grandfather's funeral.

35:22.101 --> 35:25.187
Oh, Mrs. Eom's eldest son. Hello.

35:26.020 --> 35:28.964
I should've known back then, the way you acted.

35:28.964 --> 35:31.221
Coworker, my ass.

35:31.221 --> 35:33.226
Who takes care of
a subcontractor's family like that?

35:33.226 --> 35:35.307
It was all a setup, right?

35:35.307 --> 35:38.336
I think you've got the wrong idea.
It's not like that...

35:38.336 --> 35:41.222
Wrong idea? Easy for you to say.

35:41.222 --> 35:43.926
My mom got fired. She lost everything.

35:43.926 --> 35:46.592
You'll be fine at your big company,

35:46.592 --> 35:48.808
but what about her?

35:48.808 --> 35:50.589
Let go. Let go!

35:50.589 --> 35:51.702
Sir...

35:51.702 --> 35:55.041
So you thought she was easy, you bastard?

35:58.130 --> 36:01.061
Hey, you can't do this here.

36:01.061 --> 36:03.140
Well, guess this works out perfectly.

36:03.140 --> 36:05.957
You can just step in as Dad
and take care of my family now.

36:05.957 --> 36:08.229
Sounds good, right? Dad?

36:08.229 --> 36:09.682
Sir...

36:12.496 --> 36:14.287
Let go of me.

36:14.287 --> 36:16.307
Please, just let me go.

36:16.307 --> 36:18.205
Calm down first.

36:20.273 --> 36:22.444
You went after my mom?

36:22.444 --> 36:25.221
At your age? That's just low.

36:46.595 --> 36:49.260
They say it was just stress, a one-time thing.

36:49.260 --> 36:51.532
Get some rest.

36:51.532 --> 36:54.682
Want me to grab you something to eat?

37:01.172 --> 37:02.362
Let's just go.

37:02.362 --> 37:03.643
Get some rest.

37:05.366 --> 37:07.929
I've never seen him look that helpless.

37:07.929 --> 37:10.406
He must be devastated.

37:10.406 --> 37:11.983
He acted out of kindness,

37:11.983 --> 37:15.577
and now they're calling it an affair,
making a whole scene.

37:15.577 --> 37:17.815
It's so petty, he can't even defend himself.

37:18.512 --> 37:20.324
This is just upsetting.

37:20.324 --> 37:22.909
The board's even worse now.

37:22.909 --> 37:25.519
They're saying no one would go that far
for a cafeteria lady's dad

37:25.519 --> 37:27.357
unless it's an affair.

37:27.357 --> 37:29.096
That's messed up.

37:29.096 --> 37:31.815
What's wrong with people?

37:32.520 --> 37:33.857
- Hello.
- Hi.

37:33.857 --> 37:36.497
Is Team Leader Moo in there?

37:36.497 --> 37:39.574
- Is he okay?
- Of course he's not.

37:39.574 --> 37:40.686
Any results?

37:40.686 --> 37:44.102
There's no evidence of an affair.

37:44.102 --> 37:46.574
But Head Joo is still going ahead
with disciplinary action.

37:46.574 --> 37:48.514
If it's not an affair, why punish him?

37:48.514 --> 37:50.331
There was still a disturbance at work,

37:50.331 --> 37:52.904
and it's spreading outside,
hurting the company's reputation.

37:52.904 --> 37:54.761
How is that his fault?

37:54.761 --> 37:57.494
He's the victim here. It's a witch hunt.

37:57.494 --> 38:01.237
I agree, but Head Joo...

38:01.237 --> 38:03.361
- Then...
- Hold on.

38:03.361 --> 38:06.218
He can't take another hit right now.

38:06.218 --> 38:10.015
And this disciplinary action...
we can't accept it.

38:10.015 --> 38:12.271
And what are we supposed to do if we don't?

38:12.271 --> 38:16.810
We go together, as a team,
and ask Head Joo to withdraw it.

38:16.810 --> 38:18.351
Yeah.

38:18.351 --> 38:20.136
Let's push back.

38:20.837 --> 38:22.686
I mean...

38:22.686 --> 38:24.434
it's embarrassing to say,

38:24.434 --> 38:27.471
but when I lost everything in crypto
and couldn't pay my bills,

38:27.471 --> 38:29.104
he helped me out.

38:29.104 --> 38:33.128
And when a boss is in trouble like this,
the team should have his back.

38:33.128 --> 38:36.785
If this ever happens to me,
I'll probably get treated the same.

38:36.785 --> 38:38.102
Exactly.

38:38.102 --> 38:41.602
This isn't just his problem. It's all of ours.

38:41.602 --> 38:45.240
I think things are getting a little heated.

38:45.240 --> 38:47.344
We should take a step back
and look at this rationally...

38:47.344 --> 38:49.916
So you're trying to stay out of it?

38:49.916 --> 38:54.207
Because you're the ace
and don't want to get involved?

39:04.881 --> 39:07.426
[Meet us on the rooftop! Please...]
[Team 3]

39:50.848 --> 39:54.442
Been a while since someone called me up
to the rooftop first.

39:55.183 --> 39:57.374
What is this, a gang-up?

39:57.374 --> 40:00.933
Outnumbering me feels a bit cheap.
How about a few of you step up?

40:06.871 --> 40:08.722
Ma'am.

40:08.722 --> 40:11.508
We, Team 3, are here together

40:11.508 --> 40:14.269
to speak on behalf of Team Leader Moo.

40:15.948 --> 40:19.198
Please withdraw his disciplinary action.

40:19.198 --> 40:21.222
Please withdraw it!

40:21.222 --> 40:24.153
He's already dealing with all kinds of rumors.

40:24.153 --> 40:27.959
If the discipline notice goes up,
it'll just make things worse.

40:27.959 --> 40:31.457
He didn't do anything wrong.
It was all a misunderstanding.

41:19.596 --> 41:21.641
My leg's killing me.

41:26.766 --> 41:28.590
Where were we?

41:28.590 --> 41:31.711
Right, no wrongdoing.

41:33.789 --> 41:37.027
It's true the affair hasn't been confirmed.

41:37.027 --> 41:40.464
But he did take company food off-site.

41:40.464 --> 41:43.577
And he exchanged money beyond acceptable limits
with a vendor employee.

41:43.577 --> 41:46.481
That caused issues inside
and outside the company.

41:46.481 --> 41:50.770
I'd say a reprimand sounds appropriate.

41:50.770 --> 41:54.115
Do you think people care about
all those details?

41:54.115 --> 41:55.694
They'll just see disciplinary action

41:55.694 --> 41:59.578
and assume the affair is real.

42:02.675 --> 42:06.552
And if we let it slide,
you think it'll die down?

42:06.552 --> 42:10.976
"So Audit nitpicks everyone else
but protects their own?"

42:10.976 --> 42:12.926
You don't think that'll turn into backlash?

42:12.926 --> 42:16.060
Before Head of Audit, you're our boss.

42:16.060 --> 42:17.137
If you're our boss,

42:17.137 --> 42:20.737
aren't you supposed to be a fence
for your team at times like this?

42:20.737 --> 42:24.703
If even you do this,
how are we supposed to trust this company?

42:30.900 --> 42:34.446
"Trust?" This isn't church.

42:35.219 --> 42:38.717
You work here because you get paid.

42:38.717 --> 42:41.041
You take responsibility for
what you're paid to do.

42:41.041 --> 42:44.086
Team Leader Moo answers for his.

42:49.264 --> 42:50.946
A fence?

42:51.945 --> 42:55.117
It's there to keep people
from crossing the line.

43:08.228 --> 43:10.653
White Blood Cell, that was bold.

43:10.653 --> 43:12.074
Oh no...

43:12.074 --> 43:13.816
Go on.

43:13.816 --> 43:15.985
I think we're screwed.

43:19.016 --> 43:21.360
We can't end it like this.

43:21.360 --> 43:24.017
If talks failed,

43:24.017 --> 43:25.644
we move to action.

43:25.644 --> 43:28.821
If words don't work, we show it.

43:44.223 --> 43:46.250
Excuse me.

43:46.250 --> 43:47.625
Ma'am.

43:47.625 --> 43:49.835
Looks like the team took a group half-day.

43:49.835 --> 43:52.828
Kind of a strike.

43:53.904 --> 43:56.571
They're asking you to withdraw
Team Leader Moo's discipline.

44:02.609 --> 44:05.555
There's a fly. A filthy one.

44:06.846 --> 44:09.672
Is the office not being cleaned properly?

44:12.044 --> 44:13.344
What?

44:17.180 --> 44:19.417
That's it?

44:19.417 --> 44:21.469
Okay, got it.

44:22.790 --> 44:25.270
What did she say?

44:26.454 --> 44:28.466
Nothing, really.

44:29.700 --> 44:31.111
She just swatted a fly and left.

44:31.111 --> 44:32.460
That's it?

44:32.460 --> 44:36.368
How little does she think of us
to be this unfazed?

44:36.368 --> 44:38.111
Well, that's Joo In Ah.

44:38.111 --> 44:40.397
Still not even a dent?

44:40.397 --> 44:42.842
Whatever. Let's go all in.
Burn all our leave through tomorrow.

44:42.842 --> 44:44.688
But...

44:44.688 --> 44:48.825
if she doesn't approve our leave,
isn't this just unexcused absence?

44:49.784 --> 44:54.662
Does that mean we could get disciplined too?

44:54.662 --> 44:58.352
Come on, she wouldn't go that far.

44:58.352 --> 45:01.044
Isn't that exactly what she's doing?

45:05.088 --> 45:06.680
Then...

45:06.680 --> 45:09.586
how about one of us goes up and reads the room?

45:09.586 --> 45:12.638
See where she stands.

45:12.638 --> 45:14.185
Ki Jun, want to go?

45:14.185 --> 45:15.213
Me?

45:15.213 --> 45:18.454
[Anyone know what happened
to the "Older Women Lover?"]

45:19.144 --> 45:20.565
Lastly,

45:20.565 --> 45:23.555
Executive Jeon Seong Yeol
will be returning to HQ.

45:24.158 --> 45:26.313
Please give him your full support.

45:36.380 --> 45:38.144
So it's official now.

45:38.144 --> 45:40.944
- Must be the Chairman's call.
- Of course.

45:40.944 --> 45:43.829
Man. You can't have two suns in the sky.

45:49.939 --> 45:51.914
We'll see how it plays out.

45:57.614 --> 45:59.164
Mrs. Bu.

46:03.414 --> 46:05.133
Try showing some respect.

46:06.874 --> 46:08.579
Head Bu Se Yeong.

46:09.707 --> 46:12.571
It's time you properly handle
Team Leader Moo's case.

46:12.571 --> 46:16.088
The intranet is managed by
HR's Information Office, right?

46:16.088 --> 46:20.624
We've already shared the findings...
there's no inappropriate relationship.

46:20.624 --> 46:22.208
But the board is still a mess.

46:22.208 --> 46:24.232
People are like that.

46:24.232 --> 46:27.882
- They don't care about the truth.
- Exactly.

46:27.882 --> 46:31.101
Which is why HR should be
taking things down appropriately.

46:33.246 --> 46:35.366
We're a bit busy,

46:35.962 --> 46:37.663
but we'll take a look.

46:38.295 --> 46:40.718
This is because of Executive Jeon, isn't it?

46:42.672 --> 46:44.476
Posts about him keep going up,

46:44.476 --> 46:47.369
so you're redirecting attention
and shaping public opinion.

46:47.369 --> 46:49.318
I figured as much.

46:49.318 --> 46:53.502
I was willing to let it slide, since HR is HR.

46:53.502 --> 46:54.773
But

46:55.822 --> 46:58.053
you're pushing it.

46:58.053 --> 46:59.753
"Pushing it?"

47:01.003 --> 47:03.780
What do you think HR does?

47:06.739 --> 47:08.303
Well...

47:08.303 --> 47:11.148
Though I guess it worked out for me.

47:11.148 --> 47:14.413
Rumors bury rumors, after all.

47:15.586 --> 47:17.585
Right.

47:17.585 --> 47:20.788
Rumors bury rumors, huh?

47:28.693 --> 47:31.105
What are you doing? Let go!

47:33.602 --> 47:36.657
Are you insane?

47:36.657 --> 47:38.819
Let go!

47:38.819 --> 47:40.739
Let go!

47:45.221 --> 47:47.714
Are you out of your mind?

47:55.470 --> 47:58.854
['22 New Hires Group Chat, 1 new message]
[Audit Team 3 Chat, 1 new message]

48:21.105 --> 48:24.901
What kind of person is Joo In Ah?

48:30.832 --> 48:33.880
- This is insane.
- There are already a ton of memes.

48:33.880 --> 48:36.712
- What were they even fighting about?
- They've always hated each other.

48:36.712 --> 48:38.190
It's well known.

48:39.959 --> 48:42.762
So this all went according to her plan?

48:42.762 --> 48:43.977
Right.

48:43.977 --> 48:46.916
Rumors bury rumors.

48:58.327 --> 48:59.797
Don't push it.

48:59.797 --> 49:02.806
Even a rat bites when it's cornered.

49:14.312 --> 49:15.890
Head Joo.

49:15.890 --> 49:17.979
We need to talk.

49:19.286 --> 49:21.947
Sorry, I'm closed for the day.

49:21.947 --> 49:24.960
Come to my office tomorrow.

49:24.960 --> 49:28.564
What is this complaint?
You already disciplined me.

49:28.564 --> 49:30.841
You really...

49:30.841 --> 49:33.533
trying to ruin me?

49:34.254 --> 49:36.151
Let's talk.

50:08.483 --> 50:10.416
By the way...

50:11.064 --> 50:13.641
Do you have to keep

50:13.641 --> 50:16.166
your fingers like that?

50:18.879 --> 50:21.119
To make it easier for you.

50:24.751 --> 50:27.190
Of all fingers to hurt...

50:36.589 --> 50:38.433
Alright.

50:38.433 --> 50:41.196
It's just first aid,
so get it checked out tomorrow.

50:42.178 --> 50:44.440
Since you saved me today,

50:45.423 --> 50:48.033
enjoy the meal.

50:52.173 --> 50:54.217
This is what your life's worth?

50:54.217 --> 50:56.737
Not my life. My finger.

50:57.450 --> 50:59.634
Looks edgy. Makes me look tough.

50:59.634 --> 51:01.658
I like this one.

51:01.658 --> 51:03.071
"This one?"

51:03.071 --> 51:04.597
Does this kind of thing happen a lot?

51:04.597 --> 51:06.834
This is nothing.

51:06.834 --> 51:11.811
Once, someone smashed up my entire office,
glued my chair and ran.

51:11.811 --> 51:14.497
A corrupt vendor even hit me in the head.
With a golf club.

51:14.497 --> 51:16.774
I've got a scar... somewhere here.

51:16.774 --> 51:18.191
Can you see it?

51:18.191 --> 51:19.924
That was surgery.

51:19.924 --> 51:24.495
And when I was posted overseas,
a gang threatened me with knives.

51:24.495 --> 51:26.465
So I...

51:26.465 --> 51:28.044
pulled a gun.

51:32.976 --> 51:35.187
So the "Joo Sniper" rumor...

51:35.187 --> 51:36.227
that's real?

51:36.227 --> 51:38.410
Did you actually shoot someone?

51:38.410 --> 51:40.197
What do you think?

51:42.934 --> 51:44.994
I'd rather not know.

51:54.267 --> 51:55.947
Ma'am.

51:56.973 --> 51:59.533
About earlier, with Head of HR...

52:04.718 --> 52:06.377
No, never mind.

52:12.278 --> 52:14.635
Are you a bit of a masochist?

52:14.635 --> 52:17.232
Do you enjoy being disliked?

52:17.232 --> 52:19.517
I mean, you can't avoid making enemies at work,

52:19.517 --> 52:21.709
but you can make fewer.

52:21.709 --> 52:23.953
You seem like someone

52:23.953 --> 52:25.890
who wants to be disliked.

52:25.890 --> 52:27.996
More than you really are.

52:29.488 --> 52:32.294
Who wants to be disliked?

52:32.294 --> 52:35.687
Sometimes you need to position yourself.

52:35.687 --> 52:38.597
Either be a saint or go all in as the villain.

52:38.597 --> 52:43.520
If you sit in the middle,
you get no results and lose people anyway.

52:43.520 --> 52:46.074
Do you know the worst kind of boss?

52:46.986 --> 52:48.746
The wishy-washy kind.

52:51.599 --> 52:54.132
You're definitely not that.

53:02.492 --> 53:04.715
But it must get lonely,

53:05.572 --> 53:07.660
being misunderstood.

53:11.996 --> 53:13.880
Did you misunderstand me?

53:13.880 --> 53:15.582
What kind of?

53:18.625 --> 53:20.282
I thought you were cold.

53:20.282 --> 53:24.426
Someone who'd ignore people's feelings
to get what you want.

53:26.495 --> 53:28.317
But...

53:29.750 --> 53:32.937
You have your own way

53:32.937 --> 53:35.527
of doing what you think is right.

53:37.575 --> 53:40.593
Even if it gets you misunderstood

53:40.593 --> 53:42.922
and makes things harder on you,

53:42.922 --> 53:46.520
you don't back down or make excuses.

53:48.093 --> 53:50.113
That can't be easy.

53:51.307 --> 53:53.348
Living like that...

54:03.143 --> 54:05.698
You're good with words.

54:05.698 --> 54:07.926
I'm actually a little touched.

54:10.427 --> 54:13.770
But wasn't that a bit much?

54:13.770 --> 54:15.547
You basically saw me as a psychopath.

54:15.547 --> 54:17.768
You do come off that way sometimes.

54:17.768 --> 54:19.017
Me?

54:19.017 --> 54:20.893
I love people.

54:20.893 --> 54:23.694
If I took the MBTI, I'd be an "E."
I'm like a people-loving puppy.

54:23.694 --> 54:24.857
A puppy?

54:24.857 --> 54:28.059
People find you intimidating.

54:30.386 --> 54:32.059
Don't eat that.

54:33.260 --> 54:36.923
See? This is exactly what I mean.

54:36.923 --> 54:38.949
Give it back.

54:38.949 --> 54:41.613
I'm a total psychopath, remember?

54:45.642 --> 54:48.228
Tastes better when I take it back.

54:48.228 --> 54:50.051
Hey, don't eat it all.

54:59.021 --> 55:01.531
You skipped dinner.

55:01.531 --> 55:03.421
Even if you're not hungry, have a little.

55:03.421 --> 55:05.582
Okay, just leave it.

55:12.365 --> 55:14.504
Here's the officetel key.

55:15.184 --> 55:17.402
Thank you for everything.

55:18.170 --> 55:21.556
I took a bottle of your whiskey
while I was packing.

55:21.556 --> 55:23.229
As a souvenir.

55:23.229 --> 55:24.817
That okay?

55:27.749 --> 55:29.981
That's fine, but...

55:30.706 --> 55:32.690
why all of a sudden?

55:32.690 --> 55:35.314
Is everything settled at home?

55:35.314 --> 55:37.098
No.

55:37.098 --> 55:38.543
I just...

55:40.151 --> 55:42.809
didn't want to stay there anymore.

55:44.424 --> 55:46.293
Then where are you staying?

55:46.951 --> 55:48.064
Is it safe?

55:48.064 --> 55:49.738
I'm not telling you.

55:50.618 --> 55:53.836
I want you to worry

55:53.836 --> 55:55.395
about me.

56:26.210 --> 56:28.044
Nicely wrapped.

57:31.127 --> 57:32.833
Hey!

57:52.495 --> 57:54.379
Let's see each other more often.

57:54.379 --> 57:55.684
Bro.

57:56.456 --> 57:57.817
Sure.

58:02.777 --> 58:04.701
Writing a statement again...

58:04.701 --> 58:06.919
kind of fun, in its own way.

58:12.895 --> 58:14.877
- Team Leader Moo.
- Yes?

58:14.877 --> 58:19.966
You've worked across three affiliates,
five branches, twelve teams.

58:19.966 --> 58:23.864
You know the company inside out.
Well connected, too.

58:24.483 --> 58:27.181
And for Team 3,
where dozens of posts come in daily,

58:27.181 --> 58:29.336
you're a perfect fit.

58:29.336 --> 58:30.742
Most of all,

58:30.742 --> 58:34.964
you can lead a team with strong personalities.

58:36.401 --> 58:38.658
Didn't expect a speech like that.

58:38.658 --> 58:40.552
But...

58:40.552 --> 58:42.256
it cuts both ways.

58:42.256 --> 58:47.242
That easygoing nature of yours isn't
always suitable for the leader of Audit.

58:47.242 --> 58:50.346
Other departments are subjects of audit.

58:50.346 --> 58:54.411
Use them as sources if you must,
but keep your distance.

58:56.794 --> 58:59.036
People aren't sources.

58:59.036 --> 59:00.872
They're not condiments.

59:03.652 --> 59:05.262
By the way...

59:05.262 --> 59:07.434
I did the math.

59:08.128 --> 59:13.271
On weekdays, I get maybe two hours
with my kids, tops.

59:13.271 --> 59:18.628
But I spend nine hours here
with the people at this company.

59:18.628 --> 59:24.532
If I can't be warm and friendly
with them during that time,

59:24.532 --> 59:26.489
then my life just feels

59:27.715 --> 59:30.060
kind of meaningless.

59:30.060 --> 59:33.426
If someone's struggling,

59:33.426 --> 59:35.520
I'll help however I can.

59:35.520 --> 59:39.390
If they share food, I'll gladly take it.

59:39.390 --> 59:41.911
If I have to write another statement, so be it.

59:43.643 --> 59:45.223
I'm sorry.

59:46.063 --> 59:49.356
I'm going to keep it steady.

59:49.356 --> 59:50.390
Nothing flashy.

59:50.390 --> 59:53.129
Just enjoy working here.

59:59.193 --> 01:00:02.692
If there's nothing else, I'll get going.

01:00:07.459 --> 01:00:09.309
Oh, right.

01:00:11.146 --> 01:00:15.732
Did you pull Head of HR's hair

01:00:15.732 --> 01:00:18.090
because of me?

01:00:18.883 --> 01:00:21.314
Does it matter?

01:00:21.314 --> 01:00:22.560
No.

01:00:22.560 --> 01:00:24.200
I'll get going.

01:00:32.439 --> 01:00:34.483
Maybe

01:00:34.483 --> 01:00:37.481
telling friend from foe at work

01:00:43.062 --> 01:00:45.817
isn't all that important.

01:00:49.508 --> 01:00:51.945
I won't be coming in anymore.

01:00:51.945 --> 01:00:54.490
I got a better job, so don't worry.

01:00:54.490 --> 01:00:57.762
Look at you. That's awesome.

01:00:59.405 --> 01:01:02.622
When your twins get married,
make sure you call me.

01:01:02.622 --> 01:01:05.782
I can't match you, but I'll do what I can.

01:01:05.782 --> 01:01:07.044
Of course.

01:01:11.395 --> 01:01:13.198
Take care.

01:01:13.198 --> 01:01:14.965
You too.

01:01:20.233 --> 01:01:22.861
What matters more is...

01:01:22.861 --> 01:01:25.852
[Head of Audit]

01:01:27.009 --> 01:01:29.612
Gosh, it's so dry in here.

01:01:29.612 --> 01:01:32.051
We should clean up a bit.

01:01:33.752 --> 01:01:34.819
All done?

01:01:34.819 --> 01:01:36.740
Here is your coffee, ma'am.

01:01:40.751 --> 01:01:42.934
Let me cool it for you.

01:02:01.735 --> 01:02:05.213
Having the sense
not to turn an ally into an enemy.

01:02:05.213 --> 01:02:07.891
Are you feeling hot? Want some air?

01:02:07.891 --> 01:02:10.291
- Let's crank it up.
- More?

01:02:10.920 --> 01:02:13.180
Is that better?

01:02:23.645 --> 01:02:29.885
It might be about the willingness
to stand on someone's side.

01:02:52.472 --> 01:02:56.162
Even someone like Team Leader Moo,
with a solid reputation,

01:02:56.162 --> 01:02:58.945
got cornered over a single photo.

01:03:00.244 --> 01:03:02.585
Joo In Ah's surrounded by enemies.

01:03:05.807 --> 01:03:07.851
[You've got mail]
That post...

01:03:07.851 --> 01:03:09.331
[A tip about Head of Audit Joo In Ah]
[Joo In Ah is in an inappropriate relationship]

01:03:09.331 --> 01:03:11.668
[with a coworker]
is probably a setup.

01:03:11.668 --> 01:03:12.707
Yeah.

01:03:12.707 --> 01:03:14.611
I should stop here.

01:03:48.120 --> 01:03:49.905
Excuse me.

01:03:50.973 --> 01:03:53.950
Do you need that to get in?

01:03:53.950 --> 01:03:55.340
Yes.

01:03:55.340 --> 01:03:58.967
Club members have to bring it.

01:03:58.967 --> 01:04:00.685
I see. Thanks.

01:04:07.772 --> 01:04:09.773
But...

01:04:09.773 --> 01:04:12.279
She definitely didn't have it when she went in.

01:06:44.761 --> 01:06:47.588
How am I supposed to act normal around her?

01:06:48.241 --> 01:06:49.562
This is driving me crazy.

01:06:49.562 --> 01:06:53.247
Baby, over here. Hurry.

01:06:53.247 --> 01:06:55.531
There's definitely more to this case.

01:06:55.531 --> 01:06:59.411
Who did you piss off that bad
to end up a target?

01:06:59.411 --> 01:07:02.395
If you dig into this too fast and it backfires,
you could be in trouble.

01:07:02.395 --> 01:07:03.562
Then we make sure it doesn't.

01:07:03.562 --> 01:07:04.868
Room 1306, please.

01:07:04.868 --> 01:07:06.286
I'm staying the night.

01:07:06.286 --> 01:07:09.289
Why are you hesitating?
You've already seen everything.

01:07:09.958 --> 01:07:12.187
Close your eyes for a second.
